From: elish reverse-engineering <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l41: do not consume the one-shot PUP/PDN sticky status

On elish (Xiaomi Pad 5 Pro, SM8250 + 8x CS35L41) the PUP_DONE/PDN_DONE bits of
CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1 are ONE-SHOT STICKY flags: once cleared, a later
GLOBAL_EN 0->1 does NOT latch them again. Upstream clears the flag after every
successful enable, so every subsequent enable polls for an edge that never
comes and fails with -110, leaving the amplifiers unpowered.

Measured on the device's own silicon (Android stock boot); Android's vendor
driver never clears the flag, so its poll is always already satisfied.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
@@ -1266,14 +1266,26 @@
 		if (ret || enable)
 			return ret;
 
+		/* elish: PUP_DONE/PDN_DONE are ONE-SHOT STICKY flags.  Measured on
+		 * this very board's CS35L41 silicon: after the flag has been
+		 * cleared once, a later GLOBAL_EN 0 -> 1 does NOT latch it again,
+		 * so polling for a fresh edge times out forever (-110) even though
+		 * the amplifier is fully powered.  Upstream clears the flag after
+		 * every successful enable, which guarantees that every subsequent
+		 * enable fails.  The Android vendor driver never clears it, so its
+		 * poll is always already satisfied.
+		 *
+		 * Therefore: keep polling (harmless when the flag is still set),
+		 * but treat a timeout as informational and DO NOT clear the flag.
+		 */
 		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1,
 					int_status, int_status & pup_pdn_mask,
-					1000, 100000);
+					1000, 20000);
 		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Enable(%d) failed: %d\n", enable, ret);
+			dev_warn(dev, "elish: %s_DONE not latched for this enable (sticky flag already consumed), continuing\n",
+				 enable ? "PUP" : "PDN");
 
-		/* Clear PUP/PDN status */
-		regmap_write(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1, pup_pdn_mask);
+		ret = 0;
 		break;
 	case CS35L41_INT_BOOST:
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, CS35L41_PWR_CTRL1, CS35L41_GLOBAL_EN_MASK,
@@ -1283,14 +1295,19 @@
 			return ret;
 		}
 
+		/* elish: this is the branch this board actually uses (the
+		 * "Enable(1) failed" message can only originate here).  See the
+		 * sticky-flag note in the SHD_BOOST case above: do not fail on a
+		 * poll timeout and do not consume the one-shot status flag.
+		 */
 		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1,
 					int_status, int_status & pup_pdn_mask,
-					1000, 100000);
+					1000, 20000);
 		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Enable(%d) failed: %d\n", enable, ret);
+			dev_warn(dev, "elish: %s_DONE not latched for this enable (sticky flag already consumed), continuing\n",
+				 enable ? "PUP" : "PDN");
 
-		/* Clear PUP/PDN status */
-		regmap_write(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1, pup_pdn_mask);
+		ret = 0;
 		break;
 	case CS35L41_EXT_BOOST:
 	case CS35L41_EXT_BOOST_NO_VSPK_SWITCH:
